  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5102.07 Bow Lake.\n\n(a) No person shall operate a vessel at a rate of speed in excess of 6 miles per hour on that section of Bow Lake in Strafford between:\n\n(1) The dam at the outlet of the lake;\n\n(2) The easterly point of the first island west thereof; and\n\n(3) Also on the northerly course between the easterly point of the island referred to in (2) above and the red and black buoys marking the northwest entrance to the channel.\n\nSource. #2351, eff 4-25-83; ss by #3010, eff 5-2-85; ss by #4562, eff 1-3-89; ss by #5936, INTERIM, eff 1-3-95, EXPIRES: 5-3-95 (formerly Saf-C 402.08); ss by #6005, eff 3-24-95, EXPIRED: .3-24-03\n\nNew. #7904, INTERIM, eff 6-24-03, EXPIRED: 12-21-03\n\nNew. #8107, EMERGENCY, eff 6-22-04, EXPIRES: 12-19-04; ss by #8172, eff 9-21-04; ss by #10169, EXEMPT, eff 8-8-12 (formerly Saf-C 402.07) (See Revision Note #2 at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5100)",
